---
import { getPath } from '../utils/paths';
---

<section class="py-16 bg-ocean-950/40 border-y border-white/5">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
        Engineered for Correctness
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-gray-400">
        Safe Rust rules out memory corruption. Two formal tiers then check the decisions that a broker gets wrong most expensively, and pull request CI reruns every proof and every model.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <!-- Creusot -->
      <div class="frosted-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Creusot Proof Kernels</h3>
          <span class="rounded bg-krab-500/10 border border-krab-500/30 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-krab-400">Deductive proofs</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Contracts proved on the exact executable bodies the broker calls</p>

        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-300">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-krab-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span>The <code class="font-mono text-xs text-krab-300">krabka-verified</code> crate holds small, total, allocation-light kernels. Creusot proves each one's pre- and postconditions with automated provers.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-krab-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span>KRaft vote admission and quorum size, ISR and leader failover, KIP-534 compaction retention, ACL precedence, quota token buckets, and idempotent-producer sequencing are proved kernels.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-krab-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span>Host crates call the kernel. There is no second copy of any decision, so the proved body is the one that runs.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-gray-400 border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
          Proof sessions are committed beside the code, and a pinned Creusot image redischarges every one on each pull request.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Stateright -->
      <div class="frosted-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Stateright Model Checking</h3>
          <span class="rounded bg-krab-500/10 border border-krab-500/30 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-krab-400">Exhaustive search</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Every reachable state within each model's stated bounds</p>

        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-300">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-krab-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span>Models enumerate crashes, retries, failover, replay, and concurrent operations that example-based tests cannot cover.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-krab-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span>KRaft consensus, the quorum WAL, leader failover, transactions and exactly-once, group coordination, log compaction, and client failover each have a checked model.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-krab-400 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span>Each runner pins its unique-state count. A search that shrinks without an explained model change fails the build.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-gray-400 border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
          Many models drive production decision functions directly, so the property checked is the property shipped.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 text-center">
      <a
        href={getPath('/verification')}
        class="inline-flex items-center text-sm font-semibold text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 transition-colors"
      >
        Read how Krabka is verified, and where the formal boundary ends
        <svg class="ml-1.5 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
